From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:58:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8650: let the PCIe GDSCs collapse in suspend

Same change as for SM8550: with PWRSTS_RET_ON, gdsc_disable() returns
without touching the hardware, so the PCIe controllers and PHYs stay
powered through s2idle, the sleep set has to keep a system-NoC vote for
them, and DDR never enters self-refresh. pcie-qcom turns the link off
whenever D3cold is possible and retrains it on resume, so the GDSCs can
collapse.

Link: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/commit/8dc0be9ad27c775e04bcfbc05808d60d77ddcad9
(armada packages/kernel/patches/0567-clk-qcom-gcc-sm8650-let-the-pcie-gdscs-collapse-in-suspend.patch,
committed by virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>, based on research by
@noahcdls)

Local changes (nixos-android-devices): unchanged code; regenerated against
Linux 7.3 with git headers. Applied to Aurora only, together with armada's
0522 (only endpoints veto D3cold), which it needs so that the link is
really torn down before the GDSCs collapse. Armada's SM8550 patch (0566)
is not taken. The suspend OPP floor stays (pcie_qcom.suspend_opp_floor,
default full) as a runtime fallback.
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c
@@ -3436,7 +3436,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3447,7 +3447,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3458,7 +3458,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3469,7 +3469,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
